From cd24fc53779f33103a413a03f79a092220a39030 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:25:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [Cache] swap_blocks_batch: add snapshot_src=False for
 pinned and registered H2D sources

swap_blocks_batch stages every H2D batch through a pinned buffer from the
caching host allocator, plus a host memcpy of every byte, so the caller may
reuse the source as soon as the call returns. That stays the default.

When the source is already pinned and the caller keeps it unchanged until
the copies complete, as vLLM's KV offload worker does, the snapshot only
costs: every byte is copied twice, the staging blocks stay cached in the
host allocator, and the source is read at call time instead of in stream
order.

Add a snapshot_src argument, default true. With snapshot_src=False and
every non-empty source pinned, the copies are submitted directly from the
sources. A source counts as pinned if it is USM host memory or lies inside
a range registered with xpu_host_register; SYCL reports such ranges as
usm::alloc::unknown, so hostRegister now records the ranges it registers.
Pageable sources are always staged.

Upstream: vllm-project/vllm-xpu-kernels#662
